// Five equal bars, 3:5 (the designer's 1280 by 768 image).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Queerhet flag"
  designer "kaestral (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2021-03-18"
  design-rights "The designer's post says 'Please use as you wish, no need to credit me!' This file's license covers the encoding, not the design."
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220903052522/https://kaestral.tumblr.com/post/646026078455037952/queerhet-flag"
  source "https://64.media.tumblr.com/2dc73f54373933f180736fd6b7b42243/32503dc30ddcd6c2-68/s1280x1920/a2ec57793c7595ad1bffb46dfe78bd8d12b1b284.png"
  note "Designer's own post, 'Queerhet Flag' on the Tumblr blog kaestral, dated 18 March 2021 (Wayback Machine, 3 September 2022): 'Made a queerhet flag! Queerhet - Any straight person that also exists within the LGBT community. This would include straight: Trans, Nonbinary, Intersex, Aspec, Split Attraction.' It gives no color meanings. Its first image, titled 'Flag Itself', is the flag; the others are emoji and templates made from it."
  note "Other, different flags exist for straight queer people, also called heteroqueer, such as a seven-stripe heteroqueer flag that Pride-Flags uploaded on 10 April 2021 with 'Flag by Gayer9000'. They aren't versions of this one, and aren't written here."
  note "The proportion, equal stripes and colors are read from the post's image, 1280 by 768 pixels (3:5): #5c8f9d, #7ecfa2, #7d8979, #dbcc91 and #bc766d."
}
palette {
  teal "#5c8f9d"
  green "#7ecfa2"
  grey-green "#7d8979"
  sand "#dbcc91"
  rose "#bc766d"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars teal green grey-green sand rose
